    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4da86a3a_d9a59391",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/core/ir/transform/substitute_overrides.cc",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 230,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002241
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-31T22:05:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There\u0027s no actual guarantee that instruction will appear in the allocator in dependency order. Instructions can be created and added to the module in any order. Also transforms add and remove instructions which changes this order.\n\nThis might work today due to how the AST-\u003eIR conversion process works and the fact that we don\u0027t run many heavy transforms before this point, but I\u0027m a little nervous about how fragile this is.\n\nFWIW using `if` instead of logical binary instructions would avoid this issue, as the instructions that need to be skipped would all be encapsulated inside the if blocks, which makes it easy to destroy the instructions that would be short-circuited.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 229,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 230,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "cb32a0c0d18323210edb4d82c4f58953a6e1996f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3f5e3014_4b9dee8e",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/core/ir/transform/substitute_overrides.cc",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 230,
      "author": {
        "id": 3461520
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-03T14:38:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I could traverse in control order. But your right I have to do this elaborate dead code elimination when I use these logical ops.\n\nThe challenge with the \u0027if\u0027 is that you would need to do two things.\n1. Flag the \u0027if\u0027 with a bool indicating is it compile time\n2. Guard all nested compile time \u0027if\u0027s and not evaluate them unless the parent if has been evaluated.\n\nBecause short circuiting logic is very limited #2 is likely quite doable.",
      "parentUuid": "4da86a3a_d9a59391",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 229,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 230,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "cb32a0c0d18323210edb4d82c4f58953a6e1996f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e4c01516_90674c6a",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/core/ir/transform/substitute_overrides.cc",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 230,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002241
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-03T15:20:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think #2 is straightforward if you traverse in control order (i.e. use `ir::Traverse()`), since you\u0027ll naturally evaluate the `if` statements from parent to child.",
      "parentUuid": "3f5e3014_4b9dee8e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 229,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 230,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "cb32a0c0d18323210edb4d82c4f58953a6e1996f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba57675e_8cc18fc5",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/core/ir/transform/substitute_overrides.cc",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 230,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000257
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-03T19:02:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `if` solution still feels ... wrong. The logicals are closer to what\u0027s in the original AST, and they only exist up to this transform. We can (have?) add a capabiltiy that allows the logicals.\n\nAdding `if` handling into the const evaluation is a larger task which we don\u0027t have support for at this point.",
      "parentUuid": "e4c01516_90674c6a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 229,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 230,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "cb32a0c0d18323210edb4d82c4f58953a6e1996f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ee7895c5_0bfd0573",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/core/ir/transform/substitute_overrides.cc",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 230,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002241
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-03T19:12:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMO the logical op approach feels much more \"wrong\" to me. From the tests in this CL, we have:\n```\n  %3:f32 \u003d div %one_f32, 0.0f\n  %4:bool \u003d eq %3, 0.0f\n  %5:bool \u003d logical-and %cond, %4\n```\nThe fact that %3 and %4 are actually not going to be executed based on an instruction that comes after them goes against the whole idea of the sequential execution order of instructions within a block.\n\nThe `if` approach actually captures the control flow accurately. I don\u0027t think it would be too hard to handle it in the const evaluator, in fact probably less difficult then the work that\u0027s being done in this CL for the logical approach. The main issue is adding validation support to allow it, which is non-trivial but I think very doable.",
      "parentUuid": "ba57675e_8cc18fc5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 229,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 230,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "cb32a0c0d18323210edb4d82c4f58953a6e1996f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5c2e0c77_f94be7e8",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/core/ir/transform/substitute_overrides.cc",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 230,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000257
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-03T19:22:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I can buy the feels wrong for traveling backwards reasoning. I do wonder if this means we need an `override-if` instruction in order to pick them out of the function bodies for replacement. They\u0027d, essentially, be the same as an `if` but would have to be removed during const-eval.",
      "parentUuid": "ee7895c5_0bfd0573",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 229,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 230,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "cb32a0c0d18323210edb4d82c4f58953a6e1996f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0269c0eb_6fcbb640",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/core/ir/transform/substitute_overrides.cc",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 230,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000257
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-03T19:47:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Chatted with James, we think the right way to go is to create a `consteval-if` instruction which is an `if` instruction subclass. It would require a capability to be used. It would be removed by the substitute overrides transform. It would get created for any logical-and or logical-or with the LHS as an override-expression.",
      "parentUuid": "5c2e0c77_f94be7e8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 229,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 230,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "cb32a0c0d18323210edb4d82c4f58953a6e1996f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
