      "writtenOn": "2025-01-31T22:05:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Short-circuiting override expressions inside functions also need to be handled. As it currently stands this CL does not apply validation correctly in those cases.\n\nYou could either check the LHS to see if it is an override, or just always emit these as logical operators and then replace the non-override cases with if-else instructions later.\n\nThat said, I do wonder whether it would be better/cleaner to just use `if` always. It\u0027s some extra work in the validator to allow it at module-scope under the right conditions, but I think it makes some of the `SubstituteOverride` transform simpler.",
      "revId": "cb32a0c0d18323210edb4d82c4f58953a6e1996f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
